  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nQuite a quiescent weather pattern remains in place for the\nforeseeable future. Through the work week the local \narea will be sandwiched between ridging aloft over the central \nU.S. and troughing over the Northeast. This will support general\nsurface high pressure, dry weather and seasonable temperatures.\nRidging aloft is expected to shift east this weekend, keeping \nus dry but likely allowing temperatures to trend a bit warmer.\nSplendid weather for outdoor fall activities is expected this\nweekend. Highs mainly in the 60s and lows in the 30s/40s will \nbe the general theme, though we may see some lower 70s by Sunday.\nInland locales will see additional opportunities for frost over\nthe coming nights, especially farther east. For Tuesday night \ninto Wednesday morning the greatest potential for frost looks to\nbe across far Northeast OH and Northwest PA where the growing \nseason has ended away from the lakeshore...though there will \nlikely be some frost farther west towards interior North \nCentral OH, and we may need an advisory for at least a handful \nof counties where the growing season has not been deemed \"over\".\nWill let the day shift take a better look at that potential.",
